#X text 59 405 [note] uses "Dejavu Sans Mono" as its default font \, just like Pd. But \, as of version 0.51-3 \, Pd uses 'Menlo' as its default font for macOS \, so [note] also defaults to this font in macOS., f 62;
#X text 59 450 [note] will attempt to open a font name that corresponds to your given name. If such a font name doesn't exist \, it'll open some other font you have on your system instead that it thinks is best for what you requested \, and you'll have no idea which one it is. So just be sure you have the fonts you want properly installed., f 62;
#X obj 179 314 else/note 0 50 Menlo empty 0 0 0 0 0 255 255 255 0 0 0 note;
